1. SERVICES AND SCOPE

1.1 The Service Provider agrees to provide the services described in the underlying agreement to the Client in accordance with the service levels set out in this SLA:

{{ purpose | default("Set out the services covered by this SLA.") }}

1.2 This SLA supplements, and does not replace, the underlying agreement between the Parties. In the event of inconsistency, this SLA prevails in respect of service levels and credits.


2. SERVICE LEVEL TARGETS

2.1 Availability uptime target: {{ uptime_target | default("99.9%") }}.

2.2 Response time (severity-based, during support hours): {{ response_time_hours | default("4") }} hours.

2.3 Resolution time: {{ resolution_time_hours | default("24") }} hours.

2.4 Support hours and severity levels (critical, high, medium, low):

Support hours: {{ support_hours | default("9am-5pm, Mon-Fri") }}
Severity levels and escalation: {{ severity_levels | default("Critical: service down; High: major feature impaired; Medium: minor impairment; Low: cosmetic.") }}

2.5 The service levels in this Clause 2 shall be reported and measured in accordance with the agreed measurement methodology in the underlying agreement.


3. ESCALATION AND CONTACT

3.1 Escalation contacts and notification channels: {{ escalation_contacts | default("As agreed by the Parties.") }}

3.2 The Service Provider shall notify the Client of any planned maintenance, scheduled downtime and any service-impacting incident in accordance with the agreed process.


4. SERVICE CREDITS AND REMEDIES

4.1 If the Service Provider fails to meet a service level target, the Client shall be entitled to the service credits described below, credited against future invoices:

{{ service_credits | default("As agreed by the Parties (e.g., a percentage of the monthly recurring fee per shortfall).") }}

4.2 Service credits are the sole and exclusive remedy for a failure to meet service level targets, except for failures caused by the Client, force majeure, or matters outside the Service Provider's reasonable control.


5. LIABILITY AND WARRANTY

5.1 NEITHER PARTY SHALL BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES.

5.2 Except as expressly provided, this SLA does not modify the liability cap and warranty provisions of the underlying agreement.


6. TERM AND REVIEW

6.1 This SLA shall commence on the Effective Date and continue in parallel with the underlying agreement. Auto-renew is {{ auto_renew | default("No") }}.

6.2 The Parties shall review service levels at least annually and may amend this SLA by written agreement.


7. GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTE RESOLUTION

7.1 This SLA shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of {{ governing_law | default("Sri Lanka") }}.

7.2 Any dispute arising out of or in connection with this SLA shall be resolved by {{ dispute_resolution | default("Arbitration") }} in accordance with the chosen institution's rules, and the decision shall be final and binding on the Parties.


8. GENERAL PROVISIONS

8.1 This SLA constitutes the entire agreement between the Parties regarding service levels and supersedes all prior understandings on this subject.

8.2 No amendment or waiver shall be binding unless in writing and signed by both Parties.

8.3 Notices shall be given in writing to the addresses first written above.


